{"name":"Desireé","hex":"#c4adb8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Désirée (given name)","blocks":[{"text":"Désirée, Desiree, Desirée or Desirae is a feminine given name of French origin ultimately derived from the Latin word desiderata, meaning desired. Desideria, an early version of the name and a feminine form of Desiderius, was in use in Europe as early as the 800s. The Puritans used the name Desire as a virtue name."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a5/Desiree_Clary2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C3%A9sir%C3%A9e_(given_name)","wikidata":"Q919943"},{"title":"Des'ree","blocks":[{"text":"Desirée Annette Weekes, known by her stage name Des'ree, is a British pop and soul recording artist and songwriter, who rose to prominence during the 1990s. Known for her distinctive contralto voice and uplifting lyrics, Des'ree's biggest hits include the singles \"Feel So High\", \"You Gotta Be\", and \"Life\", as well as the ballad \"Kissing You\", which featured on the soundtrack of the 1996 film Romeo + Juliet. She was named Best British Female at the 1999 Brit Awards. Her other accolades include an Ivor Novello Award, a World Music Award, and four BMI Awards."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Des'ree","wikidata":"Q258379"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Debbie Reynolds Auction - 015 - heavy silverplate inkwell, linen and lace tablecloth, and green bumblebee pillow from \"Desiree\"","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Debbie_Reynolds_Auction_-_015_-_heavy_silverplate_inkwell%2C_linen_and_lace_tablecloth%2C_and_green_bumblebee_pillow_from_%22Desiree%22.jpg/500px-Debbie_Reynolds_Auction_-_015_-_heavy_silverplate_inkwell%2C_linen_and_lace_tablecloth%2C_and_green_bumblebee_pillow_from_%22Desiree%22.jpg","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Debbie_Reyno